From 3695c63dd85f4f4a6f98ae0cd04462187aaa04f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vuln Patch Pipeline <vuln-patch@chainguard.dev>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:48:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compare password-file passwords in constant time

AbstractPasswordFilePrincipalDatabase.compareCharArray, which the
password-file principal databases use to check a supplied password
against the stored one, returned as soon as the lengths differed and
stopped at the first differing character (CWE-208, CWE-697). The time a
failed login took therefore depended on how much of the stored password
the guess matched and on whether its length was right, which lets an
attacker recover the password one character at a time.

compareCharArray now accumulates the differences across every
character of the stored value and folds a length mismatch into the
same result, so it does the same work and takes no early exit whatever
the supplied password is. An empty supplied password is compared
against the stored value itself, so it still does the full scan and is
still refused. The result of every comparison is unchanged: equal
passwords match and every other input is refused.

Adds PasswordFilePrincipalDatabaseTimingTest.

Cgp-Finding: CGP-69ph-rh6g-rg3p
